00:00:00,417 --> 00:00:02,117
One sentence from the brief:

2
00:00:02,202 --> 00:00:06,040
“Graduates working in finance in London
for more than three years”

3
00:00:06,125 --> 00:00:08,165
One sentence. Four answers.

4
00:00:08,250 --> 00:00:11,915
525 rows, for 500 members.

5
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,498
Under the loupe, London is spelled 8 ways.

6
00:00:14,583 --> 00:00:17,248
Filter the file as delivered: 2 rows.

7
00:00:17,333 --> 00:00:20,207
Normalise spellings and labels: 26.

8
00:00:20,292 --> 00:00:25,357
Merge 25 duplicates, read employers
and job titles: 49.

9
00:00:25,583 --> 00:00:26,998
But look at the dates.

10
00:00:27,083 --> 00:00:30,957
68 % of profiles: untouched
for 2 years or more.

11
00:00:31,042 --> 00:00:35,498
Three years in post and three years
without an update: the same signal.

12
00:00:35,583 --> 00:00:39,918
“340 London expats.
Twenty had moved back years ago.

13
00:00:40,003 --> 00:00:41,802
Two unsubscribed.”

14
00:00:42,042 --> 00:00:44,117
The 49 split by trust:

15
00:00:44,202 --> 00:00:47,498
1 to send, 5 to confirm,
43 to reactivate.

16
00:00:47,583 --> 00:00:49,996
6 worth contacting today.

17
00:00:50,083 --> 00:00:54,415
The administrator’s problem is not
building the list. It is believing it.

18
00:00:54,500 --> 00:00:55,985
Trusted Segments.
